          "word": "may",
          "claim": "The study examines how labeling Donald Trump as a 'convicted criminal' in Democratic political advertisements affects Democrats' views of people with criminal records and their sense of representation, and whether a counter-narrative can mitigate negative effects."
        },
        {
          "slot": "central_claim",
          "kind": "hedge",
          "word": "suggest",
          "claim": "Exposure to advertisements labeling Trump as a 'convicted criminal' negatively impacts Democrats' perceptions of people with criminal records but improves their feelings of representation; however, providing a counter-narrative featuring a system-involved representative largely mitigates the negative perceptions of people with records."
        },
        {
          "slot": "key_findings",
          "kind": "causal",
          "word": "led to",
          "claim": "The counter-narrative led to a significant decrease in support for the use of the Trump advertisement."
        },
